{"hash":"a2612d74cad30124","index":21,"payload":{"attempt":0,"kind":"RAW_PROPOSAL","raw":"Both Wt (unknown vector) \u2192 0 and Nd (unknown vector) \u2192 1 have now pruned the survivor set. Re-checking all 6 remaining hypotheses against every possible vector-assignment consistent with the data:\n\n- H21 (p1 OR NOT p2): true on all 4 remaining vectors \u2192 cannot explain Wt=0. Eliminated.\n- H09 (p1 AND NOT p2): false on all 4 remaining vectors \u2192 cannot explain Nd=1. Eliminated.\n- H00, H05, H12, H17 all survive, and working through every valid (Wt_vec, Nd_vec) assignment consistent with Wt=0, Nd=1, each of these four ends up with equal total weight \u2192 posterior is uniform 0.25 each.\n\nFor the next probe, EXPERIMENT(Qz) is unusually clean here: since the vectors already consumed by Wt and Nd under H00/H05 exhaust their \"0-outcome\" set (forcing Qz into the remaining 0-vectors), and under H12/H17 they exhaust the \"1-outcome\" set (forcing Qz into the remaining 1-vectors), the outcome at Qz is *deterministic* given which pair is true \u2014 it will split {H00,H05} (\u21920) cleanly from {H12,H17} (\u21921), regardless of the exact unknown vector Qz holds.\n\n```json\n{\"type\":\"COMMITMENT\",\"hypotheses\":{\"H00\":0.25,\"H05\":0.25,\"H12\":0.25,\"H17\":0.25},\"action\":\"EXPERIMENT(Qz)\",\"predictions\":{\"outcome=1\":0.5},\"update_kind\":\"REWEIGHT\"}\n```","ts":1787420918.7731123},"prev":"f8e389b0e2ff4046"}
